WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.825
One call gets special treatment.

2
00:00:01.825 --> 00:00:06.083
Google's REST call for organization
events is verified against Google's

3
00:00:06.083 --> 00:00:09.489
documentation, but the command-line
group for it is listed

4
00:00:09.489 --> 00:00:12.612
on the beta reference, and
its exact flags weren't read.

5
00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:16.162
So the kit marks the call
unverified, and the live invoker

6
00:00:16.162 --> 00:00:20.013
refuses to run it unless someone
passes an explicit override.

7
00:00:20.013 --> 00:00:23.849
It stays out of the scheduled run
until someone reads those flags.

8
00:00:23.849 --> 00:00:27.000
A command run on a guess
is how a read goes wrong.

9
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.346
The tests pin it: six in the
collector's Google block,

10
00:00:30.346 --> 00:00:34.320
plus the live tests for the
project command and the refusal.
